    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1084">

                <pb facs="1134" n="1014" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg1014"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">458.11 Dexter and Carpenter, Inc./82</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Sweden</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morehead</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-07-23">July 23, 1931</date>.<lb/>[Received August
                        5.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 305</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With further reference to the Department’s
                    instruction No. 54 of May 13, 1931, relating to the claim of Dexter and
                    Carpenter, Incorporated, an American corporation, against the Swedish State
                    Rail-, ways and in confirmation of my telegram No. 20 of July 22 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">21</hi>], 5 p.m.,<anchor n="10" xml:id="d1084-f1"/> I
                    have the honor to transmit herewith a copy and translation of a communication
                    received from the Minister for Foreign Affairs, dated July 18, 1931, in reply to
                    my note No. 100 of June 9th last<anchor n="10" xml:id="d1084-f2"/> informing me
                    that the Swedish Government, to its regret, cannot see its way clear to inviting
                    the Administration of the Swedish State Railways to pay a court judgment
                    rendered against it and in favor of Dexter and Carpenter, Incorporated.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John M. Morehead</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d1084-a1.xml" xpointer="d1084-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
